        "title": "Computing Pioneers - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Computing as a discipline has a peculiarly short history — from Babbage's gears to GPT-4 in under 200 years. What makes it remarkable is how densely the foundational ideas cluster in time: the entire theoretical basis was laid in roughly a single decade (1935–1945), before there was a single working computer to run any of it."
